<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33524" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palpātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A stroking</i>, <i>flattering</i>,
				<i>flattery</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aufer hinc palpationes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Men. 4, 2, 43</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Trembling</i>, <i>terror</i> (eccl.
			Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tenebrae et palpatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Isa. 32, 14</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
